<title>FRANCE: Turkey cancels barley export tender - traders.</title>
<headline>Turkey cancels barley export tender - traders.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkey has cancelled a tender for the export of 150,000 tonnes of feed barley and 50,000 tonnes of malting barley, European grain traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The barley was for shipment in February and March.  </p>
<p>&quot;They were not satisfied with the bids,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Traders did not know if or when Turkey planned to re-tender the barley.</p>
<p>There was not immediate confirmation from the Turkish Grain Board (TMO).</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5432</p>
</text>
